0,Hmu language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hmu_language,"The Hmu language (hveb Hmub), also known as Qiandong Miao (黔东, Eastern Guizhou Miao), Central Miao (中部苗语), East Hmongic (Ratliff 2010 [1]), or (somewhat ambiguously) Black Miao, is a dialect cluster of Hmongic languages of China.","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
1,Hmong-Mien languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hmong–Mien_languages,"The Hmong-Mien languages (also known as Miao-Yao and rarely as Yangtzean) [1] are a highly tonal language family of southern China and northern Southeast Asia. They are spoken in mountainous areas of southern China, including Guizhou, Hunan, Yunnan, Sichuan, Guangxi, Guangdong and Hubei provinces. The speakers of these languages are predominantly ""hill people"", in contrast to the ...","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
2,"Miao People's Ancient Ethnic Song ""Maple Song"" | Chinese Ethnic Music",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b83_E2mrPCw,"The Miao are a group of linguistically related peoples living in Southern China and Southeast Asia, who are recognized by the government of China as one of the 56 official ethnic groups.","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
3,Miao (Hmong) Music (music genre) | WorldMusic,https://worldmusic.heuron.com/en/genres/miao-music,"How it came about The Miao/Hmong are an Indigenous people distributed across southern China (Guizhou, Yunnan, Hunan), northern Laos, Vietnam, Thailand, and Burma, with significant 20th-century diaspora to the US, France, and Australia after the Vietnam War era. The music is tied to agricultural ritual, courtship gatherings, and seasonal festivals. Oral transmission has carried the tradition ...","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
4,"Miao, Southern Qiandong Language (HMS) - Ethnologue",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/hms/,"Miao, Southern Qiandong Summary Southern Qiandong Miao is a stable indigenous language of China. It belongs to the Hmong-Mien language family and is part of the Hmong macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools ...","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
5,Miao Traditional Festival Concert #hmong - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pTbErlec_u4,Miao Traditional Festival Concert #hmong 幽谷琴聲 Silent Valley 922 subscribers Subscribe,"Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
6,Hmong Folk Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/hmong-folk-music,"Hmong folk music is the traditional musical expression of the Hmong (Miao) people, whose communities historically lived in the mountainous regions of southern China and later migrated across mainland Southeast Asia. It centers on an oral, community-based practice linked to ritual, storytelling, courtship, and seasonal festivities.","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
7,Southern-Qiandong-Miao / Rongshui Miao - lingweb.eva.mpg.de,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Miao-Southern-Qiandong.htm,"Southern Qiandong Miao. Alternates: Black Miao, Central Miao, Chientung Miao, Hei Miao, Hmu, Southern East-Guizhou Miao, Southern Hmu), is spoken by approximately 500,000 speakers (Wang and Mao 1995) in Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region: Rongshui and Sanjiang counties; Guizhou province: Danzhai, Libo, Rongjiang Congjiang, and Sandu counties, China.","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
8,OLAC resources in and about the Southern Qiandong Miao language,http://www.language-archives.org/language/hms,"Other known names and dialect names: Black Miao, Central Miao, Chientung Miao, Hei Miao, Hmu, Southern Qiandong Miao, Southern East-Guizhou Miao, Southern Hmu Other search terms: dialect, vernacular, lexicon, dictionary, vocabulary, wordlist, phrase book, grammar, syntax, morphology, phonology, orthography","Miao, Southern Qiandong",Hmong-Mien
